# Frontend build configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and edit. Nothing here is required: with no `.env` file at
# all the app runs against its in-memory service layer and needs no backend.

# Which service implementation is live.
#
#   local - in-memory, seeded from src/data/mock.ts. Default. No backend needed.
#   http  - the .NET 10 API in dotnet-api/, which owns paging, filtering,
#           sorting and every business rule.
VITE_API_MODE=local

# Base URL of the .NET 10 API. Only read when VITE_API_MODE=http.
# Must match the origin the API's Cors:AllowedOrigins permits.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5199

# Start the API first:
#
#   cd ../dotnet-api/src/RecordRoom.Api
#   dotnet run --urls http://localhost:5199
#
# It applies migrations and seeds the demo dataset on startup if the registry is
# empty. Demo logins all use the password Demo@12345: admin, supervisor,
# operator, employee.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Barcode features (record-room section)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The product is a Document Management System. The record room (physical file
# tracking, rooms and shelves) is an additional section of it, and barcodes belong
# to that section only. This switch turns the barcode part on or off.
#
#   true  - barcode scanning, labels and barcode values are available.
#   false (default) - they are hidden; files are identified by FILE NUMBER.
#                     Accepted "off" values: false, 0, off, no, disabled.
#
# In http mode the API's own setting (Features__BarcodeEnabled, served at
# GET /api/config) wins over this value, so set both to the same thing. The
# deploy script defaults the API flags to false and preserves operator choices.
# In local mode these VITE_ENABLE_* values are the only source.
VITE_ENABLE_BARCODE=false
VITE_ENABLE_MOVEMENT=false
VITE_ENABLE_SUPPORT=false
VITE_ENABLE_BULK_IMPORT=false

# The approved proposal scope keeps these existing capabilities visible:
# file registry, maps, scan upload/review, custody register, issue/return,
# reports, accounts/settings and the audit history.
#
# These retained optional capabilities are hidden unless explicitly enabled:
# - Barcode workflows: VITE_ENABLE_BARCODE / Features__BarcodeEnabled
# - Standalone movement log and report: VITE_ENABLE_MOVEMENT / Features__MovementEnabled
# - Support, inquiries and media links: VITE_ENABLE_SUPPORT / Features__SupportEnabled
# - Bulk import: VITE_ENABLE_BULK_IMPORT / Features__BulkImportEnabled
#
# What VITE_ENABLE_BARCODE=false hides or changes, page by page
# (everything else in the record room - issue, return, movement, rooms - stays):
#
#   Menu / navigation
#     - "Scan a barcode" tab (Record room > Issue & return) and /scan route
#     - "Barcode labels" tab (Record room > Rooms) and /barcodes route
#     - Mobile bottom bar: the Scan tab is replaced by Digitization
#     - Top-bar search hint no longer mentions barcodes
#   Documents (file table)
#     - Barcode line under each file number; barcode in the CSV export
#     - Row menu: "Copy barcode" and "Print barcode label"
#     - Search hint no longer mentions barcodes
#   File viewer and file details
#     - Barcode field and barcode image; "Print label" action
#   Register file
#     - Barcode field and barcode preview (an internal id is still generated)
#   Maps
#     - File barcode shown in the table and pickers (the file number is used)
#   Issue files
#     - The scan-a-barcode box; files are added by searching file number or subject
#   Return files and Search
#     - Barcode values and "barcode" search hints
#   Record rooms (room detail)
#     - Shelf and almirah barcode values
#   Room layout (administration)
#     - Barcode inputs and values for almirahs and shelves
#   Digitization
#     - "Registry barcode" becomes "File number" when adding a page
#   Bulk import
#     - Columns are labelled "File ID" and "Shelf ID" instead of barcode
#   Permissions
#     - barcodes.print has no effect while the switch is off


# Retained modules outside the current approved scope. Enable explicitly when required.

# Dashboard percentages use department-approved denominators. Do not set these
# values until the Department signs off the inventory and page volumes.
# API environment keys: Scope__ExpectedFileCount and Scope__ExpectedPageCount.
# Until configured, mapped/digitization progress reports 0% rather than inventing a denominator.
